#usda 1.0
(
    """
    In this museum case, /Root references lib.usda</Asset>, which
    specializes /_class_Lib.  /_class_Lib/Model/InheritsMat inherits
    /_class_Lib/_class_Mat, so /Root/Model/InheritsMat has an implied
    inherit to lib.usda</Asset/_class_Mat>, which provides the attribute
    fromAssetClass and the child prim Kid.  /Root/Model/SpecializesMat is
    the same with a specializes instead of an inherit.

    Asset/Model has no specs, so in the prim index for /Root/Model the
    only node under the reference to lib.usda</Asset/Model> is the inert
    placeholder for the specializes to /_class_Lib/Model, whose opinions
    are provided by the propagated node under the root.  The implied
    classes for InheritsMat and SpecializesMat are evaluated through that
    placeholder and implied under the reference node, at
    lib.usda</Asset/_class_Mat>.

    Previously the placeholder, and then the reference node, were culled
    in /Root/Model.  The implied inherit to lib.usda</Asset/_class_Mat>
    was then added beneath the culled reference node, and child name
    composition skipped it, so Kid was missing from
    /Root/Model/InheritsMat.  For SpecializesMat the implied node is a
    placeholder whose opinions are provided under the root, so the results
    were right, but the index still had a node beneath a culled parent
    that was not culled itself.  We expect Kid under both.
    """
)

def "Root" (
    references = @./lib.usda@</Asset>
)
{
}
